61	78	262	Dr Arun Sharma	arunsharma@igdtuw.ac.in	external	academic	2026-07-28 11:51:09.643869	SOCSEA	SUBMITTED	2026-07-30 19:36:25.689236	{"schoolName":"School of Computer Science Engineering & Applications","establishmentYear":"2018","address":"D Y Patil International University\\\\nSector 29, Nigdi Pradhikaran, Akurdi, Pune, Maharashtra 411044","directorName":"Prof. (Dr.) Rahul Sharma","directorEmail":"rahul.sharma@dypiu.ac.in","ugIntake":"1420","pgIntake":"120","academicCalendar":"Available","bosMeetingsCount":"2","stakeholderFeedback":"Stakeholder Feedback Analysis Folder Link: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1MkDXTuTEsrZ5R7VosWEqBdwlKv34_QlF?usp=drive_link\\\\nThis folder contains feedback-related documents for the following stakeholders: Alumni, Academic Peers, Faculty Members, Students, Parents, and Employers.\\\\nThe folder includes:\\\\n1. Sample feedback forms collected from each stakeholder group.\\\\n2. Feedback Analysis Reports and Action Taken Reports (ATRs) based on the feedback received.","feedbackAnalysis":"Stakeholder Feedback Analysis Folder Link: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1MkDXTuTEsrZ5R7VosWEqBdwlKv34_QlF?usp=drive_link\\\\nThis folder contains feedback-related documents for the following stakeholders: Alumni, Academic Peers, Faculty Members, Students, Parents, and Employers.\\\\nThe folder includes:\\\\n1. Sample feedback forms collected from each stakeholder group.\\\\n2. Feedback Analysis Reports and Action Taken Reports (ATRs) based on the feedback received.","actionTakenReport":"Stakeholder Feedback Analysis Folder Link: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1MkDXTuTEsrZ5R7VosWEqBdwlKv34_QlF?usp=drive_link\\\\nThis folder contains feedback-related documents for the following stakeholders: Alumni, Academic Peers, Faculty Members, Students, Parents, and Employers.\\\\nThe folder includes:\\\\n1. Sample feedback forms collected from each stakeholder group.\\\\n2. Feedback Analysis Reports and Action Taken Reports (ATRs) based on the feedback received.","foreignCollaborations":"The School has consistently promoted research through publications in reputed\\\\ninternational journals during the academic years 2025–2026. Faculty members have\\\\npublished more than 40 research papers in internationally recognized journals and\\\\npublishers, including Nature Scientific Reports, Springer, IEEE, Elsevier (Science\\\\nDirect), Wiley, World Scientific, Frontiers in Artificial Intelligence, AI, and\\\\nComputational Biology and Chemistry. Several publications are co-authored with\\\\nresearchers from other institutions, reflecting collaborative research practices and\\\\ninterdisciplinary engagement. The research covers emerging areas such as Artificial\\\\nIntelligence, Machine Learning, Cyber Security, Internet of Things (IoT), Renewable\\\\nEnergy, Medical Image Processing, Smart Agriculture, Wireless Communication, and\\\\nApplied Mathematics.\\\\nExp: School of Engineering, Swinburne University of Technology, Hawthorn, Australia\\\\nhttps://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-22310-w","nationalCollaborations":"The School has established active research collaborations with several national\\\\ninstitutions through joint research publications and conference proceedings during the\\\\nacademic years 2025–2026. Faculty members have collaborated with researchers from\\\\nreputed Indian universities, engineering colleges, research organizations, and industry\\\\npartners, These collaborative research efforts span interdisciplinary domains such as\\\\nArtificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Cyber Security, Internet of Things (IoT),\\\\nRenewable Energy, Healthcare, Wireless Communication, and Applied Mathematics.\\\\nThe collaborations have strengthened the institution&#39;s research ecosystem, promoted\\\\nknowledge sharing, enhanced publication quality, and facilitated interdisciplinary\\\\nresearch at the national level.\\\\nExp: VIT, Vellore, Symbiosis International (Deemed University)\\\\nhttps://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11299572\\\\nhttps://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-04591-3","functionalMousCount":"4","auditObservations":"The School of Computer Science Engineering & Applications has established the necessary academic framework for delivering its programs and offers curricula aligned with contemporary computing disciplines. The School has initiated several quality assurance practices and academic processes. Number of Admissions in various programs are very good.","auditRecommendations":"a number of key areas require focused attention to enhance academic effectiveness and institutional quality. During the audit, it was observed that the Vision and Mission statements of the School do not adequately reflect the distinct purpose of each. The Vision statement does not clearly articulate the long-term aspirations and future direction of the School, while the Mission statements are not sufficiently aligned with the strategies and actions required to achieve the envisioned goals.\\n\\nThe implementation of Outcome-Based Education (OBE) also requires significant strengthening. The CO–PO mapping needs a more systematic and rationale-based approach to ensure comprehensive coverage of all Program Outcomes and Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs). It was observed that one of the PSOs was not mapped with any course, indicating gaps in curriculum alignment. Academic records relating to student intake and admissions require greater clarity, as sanctioned intake against actual admissions was not consistently reflected in the available documentation. The School also needs to improve its performance in key academic quality indicators, particularly faculty research publications and student progression in terms of placements, higher education, and entrepreneurship. Further, the Student–Faculty Ratio (SFR) for the academic year 2025–26 was observed to be significantly higher than desirable (approximately 92:1), which may adversely affect effective teaching-learning processes, mentoring, and student engagement. The documented best practices also require refinement to better demonstrate innovation, measurable outcomes, scalability, and their contribution to institutional quality enhancement.","auditDocumentation":[],"__reportArchive":{"category":"internal","auditCycle":"2025-26","version":1},"__auditSignOff":{"submittedBy":{"name":"Dr Rahul Sharma","designation":"Director","role":"director","date":"2026-07-28T11:40:44.670Z"},"approvedBy":{"name":"","designation":"","role":"","date":""},"auditedBy":{"name":"Dr Arun Sharma","designation":"External Academic Auditor","role":"academic-external-auditor","email":"arunsharma@igdtuw.ac.in","date":"2026-07-30T19:36:22.890Z"}}}	{"studentStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Class":"FY B.Tech CSE","No. of Student":"1275","Total":"2840"},{"Sr No":"2","Class":"SY B.Tech CSE","No. of Student":"702","Total":"2840"},{"Sr No":"3","Class":"TY B.Tech CSE","No. of Student":"494","Total":"2840"},{"Sr No":"4","Class":"FIY B.Tech CSE","No. of Student":"369","Total":"2840"},{"Sr No":"5","Class":"FY BCA","No. of Student":"98","Total":"272"},{"Sr No":"6","Class":"SY BCA","No. of Student":"62","Total":"272"},{"Sr No":"7","Class":"TY BCA","No. of Student":"112","Total":"272"},{"Sr No":"8","Class":"FY MCA","No. of Student":"120","Total":"177"},{"Sr No":"9","Class":"SY MCA","No. of Student":"57","Total":"177"}],"facultyStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Required":"137 (On the basis of SFR 1:24)","Available":"36 (As on 10 July 2025 After new Appointments- 64)"}],"boardOfStudies":[{"Sr No":"1","Date of the meeting":"28/11/2025","Link for MoM":[{"name":"9th_SoCSEA_BoS_MoM_28_11_2025.pdf","fileName":"9th_SoCSEA_BoS_MoM_28_11_2025.pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/ee77228d84fc13f0/attachments/f6bafe4c-198b-49d2-95cb-3f5011ae2591-9th_SoCSEA_BoS_MoM_28_11_2025.pdf"}]},{"Sr No":"2","Date of the meeting":"11/04/2026","Link for MoM":[{"name":"10th_SoCSEA_BoS_MoM_11_04_2026.pdf","fileName":"10th_