41	72	262	Dr Arun Sharma	arunsharma@igdtuw.ac.in	external	academic	2026-07-28 11:15:11.183178	SOCM	SUBMITTED	2026-07-30 19:43:55.438032	{"schoolName":"School of Commerce and Management","establishmentYear":"2018","address":"Akurdi, Pune","directorName":"Dr. Madhavi Deshpande","directorEmail":"madhavi.deshpande@dypiu.ac.in","ugIntake":"120","pgIntake":"60","academicCalendar":"Available","bosMeetingsCount":"02","stakeholderFeedback":"Feedback on the curriculum was collected from various stakeholders, including academic peers, industry experts, alumni, employers, faculty members,  during the Academic Year 2025–26. Overall, stakeholders appreciated that the curriculum is contemporary, outcome-based, and aligned with industry requirements. They acknowledged the inclusion of emerging areas such as Artificial Intelligence, Business Analytics, Digital Marketing, Sustainability, FinTech, and Industry 4.0/5.0.","feedbackAnalysis":"The feedback was analysed by the Programme Assessment Committee (PAC) and discussed in the Board of Studies (BoS) meetings. The analysis indicated that while the curriculum is relevant and industry-oriented, continuous improvement is essential to meet evolving business and technological requirements.","actionTakenReport":"Based on feedback received from academic peers, alumni, and parents, the School of Commerce and Management undertook several quality enhancement initiatives. The curriculum was reviewed and updated through Board of Studies (BoS) meetings by incorporating academic and industry inputs, with greater emphasis on emerging technologies, practical and experiential learning, and industry relevance. Internship mentoring, industry interactions, guest lectures, workshops, and placement readiness activities were strengthened to enhance students' employability and professional competencies. In addition, the mentor-mentee system, remedial support, counselling, faculty development programmes, and campus facilities were reinforced to improve student learning, well-being, and overall stakeholder satisfaction.","foreignCollaborations":"00","nationalCollaborations":"05","functionalMousCount":"05","auditObservations":"The School of Commerce and Management (SoCM) has established a conducive academic environment supported by a satisfactory Student–Faculty Ratio, enabling effective teaching-learning, student mentoring, and academic engagement. The academic and administrative documentation is generally comprehensive and well maintained, reflecting adherence to institutional processes and quality assurance practices. The School has initiated several academic and quality enhancement activities; however, certain aspects require further strengthening to improve their overall effectiveness and impact.","auditRecommendations":"During the audit, it was observed that the implementation of Outcome-Based Education (OBE) requires further improvement, particularly in strengthening faculty understanding of outcome formulation, CO–PO mapping, attainment analysis, and the use of attainment data for continuous quality improvement. The mechanism for identifying slow and advanced learners, along with the corresponding intervention strategies and Action Taken Reports (ATRs), lacks a clearly defined framework and adequate evidence of systematic implementation. Although placement initiatives are being undertaken, the overall placement performance remains moderate and warrants focused efforts to enhance graduate employability. Furthermore, the documented best practices require refinement to better demonstrate their distinctiveness, measurable outcomes, sustainability, and contribution towards academic and institutional excellence. Further, international academic collaborations, particularly in the domain of management education, are presently limited and require greater emphasis to provide students and faculty with enhanced global exposure and opportunities for collaborative teaching, research, and academic exchange.","auditDocumentation":[],"__reportArchive":{"category":"internal","auditCycle":"2025-26","version":1},"__auditSignOff":{"submittedBy":{"name":"Dr Madhavi Deshpande","designation":"Director","role":"director","date":"2026-07-25T08:05:14.019Z"},"approvedBy":{"name":"","designation":"","role":"","date":""},"auditedBy":{"name":"Dr Arun Sharma","designation":"External Academic Auditor","role":"academic-external-auditor","email":"arunsharma@igdtuw.ac.in","date":"2026-07-30T19:43:53.336Z"}}}	{"studentStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Class":"BBA Batch 2025-29","No. of Student":"126","Total":"126"},{"Sr No":"2","Class":"BBA Batch 2024-28","No. of Student":"89","Total":"89"},{"Sr No":"3","Class":"BBA Batch 2023-27","No. of Student":"102","Total":"102"},{"Sr No":"4","Class":"MBA Batch 2025-27","No. of Student":"58","Total":"58"},{"Sr No":"5","Class":"MBA Batch 2024-26","No. of Student":"50","Total":"50"}],"facultyStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Required":"24","Available":"17"}],"boardOfStudies":[{"Sr No":"1","Date of the meeting":"9-4-2025 and 6-11-2025 ","Link for MoM":[{"name":"SoCM BOS SUMMARY_Updated (1).pdf","fileName":"SoCM BOS SUMMARY_Updated (1).pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/3dcc0dd157752392/attachments/b265ffe5-a905-4763-a465-c462a635c24f-SoCM_BOS_SUMMARY_Updated__1_.pdf"}]}],"syllabusRevision":[{"Sr No":"1","Category of Feedback":"Academic peer Feedback  Analysis and ATR","Link for Analysis and ATR":[{"name":"Academic Peer Feedback and ATR (1) - Copy (1).pdf","fileName":"Academic Peer Feedback and ATR (1) - Copy (1).pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/3dcc0dd157752392/attachments/efa1d864-6814-4558-848a-84282b28add8-Academic_Peer_Feedback_and_ATR__1__-_Copy__1_.pdf"},{"name":"Academic Peer Feedback and ATR (1) (3).pdf","fileName":"Academic Peer Feedback and ATR (1) (3).pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/3dcc0dd157752392/attachments/2931a976-140d-481a-82b0-fb96f18eef00