42	71	263	Dr Abhijeet Digalwar	akd@pilani.bits-pilani.ac.in	external	academic	2026-07-28 11:15:18.661337	SOEMR	SUBMITTED	2026-08-13 04:53:10.323798	{"schoolName":"School of Engineering, Management and Research (SEMR)","establishmentYear":"2024","address":"Sector 29, Nigdi Pradhikaran, Akurdi, Pune, Maharashtra 411044","directorName":"Dr. Mrs. Anupama V Patil","directorEmail":"anupama.patil@dypiu.ac.in","ugIntake":"360","pgIntake":"nil","academicCalendar":"Available","bosMeetingsCount":"08","stakeholderFeedback":"Feedback was collected from parents, students, faculty members, and academic peers regarding the curriculum and learning environment. Overall, stakeholders appreciated the relevance of the curriculum and teaching-learning process while recommending greater emphasis on industry-oriented content, practical and project-based learning, emerging technologies, internships, skill development, improved infrastructure, and stronger industry-academia interaction to enhance students' employability and holistic development.","feedbackAnalysis":"Feedback was collected from parents, students, faculty members, and academic peers regarding the curriculum and learning environment. Overall, stakeholders appreciated the relevance of the curriculum and teaching-learning process while recommending greater emphasis on industry-oriented content, practical and project-based learning, emerging technologies, internships, skill development, improved infrastructure, and stronger industry-academia interaction to enhance students' employability and holistic development.","actionTakenReport":"Based on the stakeholder feedback, the department strengthened industry-institute interaction through industrial visits, expert lectures, internships, and MoUs with industries. Project-based learning, mini-projects, and value-added certification courses were encouraged, while practical components, case studies, and emerging technologies were integrated into course delivery. The institute also upgraded laboratory facilities, library resources, and digital infrastructure to provide a better learning environment and support continuous curriculum improvement.","foreignCollaborations":"2","nationalCollaborations":"6","functionalMousCount":"12","auditObservations":"The School of Engineering, Management and Research has established a sound academic ecosystem with qualified faculty members, adequate teaching-learning infrastructure, and well-equipped laboratories supporting engineering education and research. The School has initiated several quality assurance practices and offers programmes aligned with current technological and managerial requirements. Industry interaction through guest lectures, internships, industrial visits, and collaborative activities has contributed positively to experiential learning. The School also demonstrates encouraging initiatives in promoting innovation, entrepreneurship, and multidisciplinary education through project-based learning and student participation in technical competitions. The academic and administrative documentation is generally satisfactory and reflects adherence to institutional processes. However, there remains considerable scope for further strengthening several academic quality parameters to achieve national and international benchmarks.","auditRecommendations":"• Strengthen the implementation of Outcome-Based Education (OBE) by improving faculty understanding of outcome formulation, CO–PO/PSO mapping, attainment analysis, and systematic use of attainment results for continuous quality improvement.\\n• Revise the Vision and Mission statements, where necessary, to clearly differentiate the School's long-term aspirations from its strategic objectives and ensure alignment with institutional goals.\\n• Enhance curriculum enrichment by incorporating emerging areas such as Artificial Intelligence, Industry 5.0, Digital Manufacturing, Data Analytics, Sustainability, Smart Systems, and Business Analytics.\\n• Increase interdisciplinary teaching and collaborative projects integrating engineering, management, design, and biosciences.\\n• Improve research productivity by encouraging quality publications in high-impact journals, sponsored research projects, patents, technology transfer, and consultancy.\\n• Strengthen industry partnerships for curriculum development, internships, live projects, professor of practice, adjunct faculty engagement, and collaborative research.\\n• Improve graduate employability through structured skill-development programmes, industry certifications, placement training, and entrepreneurship support.\\n• Strengthen faculty development initiatives focusing on modern pedagogy, digital learning, research methodologies, and international collaborations.\\n• Develop measurable Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) for annual academic review and continuous institutional improvement.","auditDocumentation":[],"__reportArchive":{"category":"internal","auditCycle":"2025-26","version":1},"__auditSignOff":{"submittedBy":{"name":"Dr Anupama Patil","designation":"Director","role":"director","date":"2026-07-24T07:30:32.402Z"},"approvedBy":{"name":"","designation":"","role":"","date":""},"auditedBy":{"name":"Dr Abhijeet Digalwar","designation":"External Academic Auditor","role":"academic-external-auditor","email":"akd@pilani.bits-pilani.ac.in","date":"2026-08-13T04:53:10.335Z"}}}	{"studentStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Class":"F.Y Mechanical Engineering","No. of Student":"118","Total":"118"},{"Sr No":"2","Class":"S.Y Mechanical Engineering","No. of Student":"106","Total":"106"},{"Sr No":"3","Class":"T.Y Mechanical Engineering","No. of Student":"24","Total":"24"},{"Sr No":"4","Class":"F.Y Semiconductor Engineering","No. of Student":"76","Total":"76"},{"Sr No":"5","Class":"S.Y Semiconductor Engineering","No. of Student":"71","Total":"71"},{"Sr No":"6","Class":"F.Y Chemical Engineering","No. of Student":"52","Total":"52"},{"Sr No":"7","Class":"S.Y Chemical Engineering","No. of Student":"21",