"(iv) Total Activities":"","All Students List Attachment":[{"name":"B. Tech Bio Medical.pdf","fileName":"B. Tech Bio Medical.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/ac0fbdbd045b25d0/attachments/f4071bb1-078e-4437-8c12-392247d403dd-B._Tech_Bio_Medical.pdf"}],"Certificates Attachment":""},{"Sr No":"3","Activity":"B. Tech Bio Chemical ","(i) Number of Organizations":"","(ii) Number of Students":"31","(iii) Activities with Stipend":"","(iv) Total Activities":"","All Students List Attachment":[{"name":"B. Tech BioChem.pdf","fileName":"B. Tech BioChem.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/ac0fbdbd045b25d0/attachments/7e4b6b2d-f386-419a-b317-224e3c7c20a2-B._Tech_BioChem.pdf"}],"Certificates Attachment":""}],"careerGuidanceActivities":[{"Sr No":"1","Title of the Session":"","Name of the Resource Person":"","Date of Conduction":"","No. of Beneficiaries":"","Link for Proofs":""}],"industryInteractionActivities":[{"Sr No":"1","Title of the Session":"","Name of the Resource Person":"","Date of Conduction":"","No. of Beneficiaries":"","Link for Proofs":""}],"otherActivities":[{"Sr No":"1","Title of the Session":"","Name of the Resource Person":"","Date of Conduction":"","No. of Beneficiaries":"","Link for Proofs":""}],"trainingActivities":[{"Sr No":"1","Academic Year":"2025-2026","Title of the Event":"Professional Skills Course","Date of Conduction":"29th Jan 2026 to 10th April 2026","No. of Students Benefited":"328","Attachment":[{"name":"C_B.Tech SoEMR_Skill Development_Final Report 2026.pdf","fileName":"C_B.Tech SoEMR_Skill Development_Final Report 2026.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/ac0fbdbd045b25d0/attachments/c89a98f1-af12-41c2-882a-16ed372cefb4-C_B.Tech_SoEMR_Skill_Development_Final_Report_2026.pdf"},{"name":"C_B.Tech SoEMR_Skill Development_Final Report 2026 (1).pdf","fileName":"C_B.Tech SoEMR_Skill Development_Final Report 2026 (1).pdf","url":"/uploads/users/ac0fbdbd045b25d0/attachments/f58696e8-6e1f-40ed-af0b-73fc3129a755-C_B.Tech_SoEMR_Skill_Development_Final_Report_2026__1_.pdf"}]}],"industryCollaborations":[{"Sr No":"1","Organization / Institution / Industry":"","Year of Signing MoU":"","Duration of MoU":"","Activities Conducted Under the MoU":"","Attachment":""}]}],"auditObservations":"•\\tAdministrative Welfare Initiatives: The administrative department has proactively implemented multiple policies and welfare measures to support both  faculty and students.\\n•\\tCommittee Documentation & Outcomes: While meeting minutes for statutory bodies (including the ICC, Grievance Cell, and Anti-Ragging Committee) are well-documented, the specific actions taken based on their recommendations must be clearly presented as measurable outcomes.\\n•\\tQuality Audits: The institution has successfully executed several key quality assurance initiatives, maintaining records for Energy, Environmental, Green, Gender, and Library audits.\\n•\\tScholarship Visibility: Current scholarship documentation only highlights internal (in-house) awards. Information regarding external and non-university scholarships needs to be made visible if available.\\n•\\tFaculty-Student Ratio (FSR): A comprehensive list of faculty and staff, detailing their professional experience, is available; however, the university needs to focus on improving its overall Faculty-Student Ratio.\\n•\\tInfrastructure & Resources: The review confirms the availability of excellent infrastructure, which includes robust physical and digital library resources.\\n•\\tStudent Activities: A strong variety of student activities is evident, though the formal documentation and recording of these events require improvement.\\n•\\tSports Achievements: The report reflects a commendable number of awards and recognitions achieved by students across various sports.\\n•\\tPlacement & Industry Collaboration: The CRPC provided data on training activities, industry collaborations, and placements. Moving forward, the actual outcomes and conversion rates of these initiatives need significant enhancement.\\n","auditRecommendations":"Administrative office and HR :-\\n\\n•\\tEstablish a structured institutional reporting framework covering scholarships, EWS fee concessions, digital HR integration, health insurance, maternity and paternity leave, faculty experience, retention, and faculty development benefits. \\n•\\tEnsure Faculty Grievance, SC-ST, and Anti-Ragging Cells conduct regular documented meetings, even when no cases are reported throughout the year.\\n•\\tMaintain an audit action-taken register capturing every recommendation, corrective measure, responsibility, timeline, and evidence of closure. \\n•\\tThe review indicates several strong practices, but documentation, consistency, and outcome tracking require improvement. Scholarship provisions need clarity on whether budgets are fixed or revised annually, while EWS support should be formally recorded.\\n•\\tFaculty data should include total and institutional experience, retention rates, benefits, health insurance, and leave policies.\\n\\nLibrary  :-\\n•\\tLibrary online and offline resources are available. Need to showcase outcome in terms of utilization and usage reports from vendors. \\n•\\tUse of e books can be shown as SDG initiative of the university\\n\\nCorporate Relations and Placement cell (Office of Career Services):- \\n•\\tFor placements, map each activity and initiative with measurable outcomes, including student participation, skill improvement, internship conversion, and placement performance.\\n•\\tCRPC / OCS should document Industry inputs and provide the feedback to the school, wherever relevant, for both incoming and existing batches in a structured manner.\\n•\\tStrengthen industry linkages beyond MoUs through internships, live projects, expert sessions, consultancy, research collaborations, and industry visits. \\n\\nStudent Welfare :-\\n•\\tStudent Welfare should maintain annual budgets, activity calendars, counselling records, mentorship outcomes, sports schedules, and consolidated yearly reports or magazines. \\n•\\tDevelop a comprehensive alumni database, actively engage alumni for mentoring, networking, placements, and fund generation. \\n•\\tStudent welfare initiatives require stronger records, annual calendars, counselling outcomes, grievance mechanisms, statutory cell meetings, and consolidated reporting.\\n•\\tEfforts to be made to provide scholarships from Industry / NGOs and other private organizations for needy students.\\n•\\tAlumni engagement and industry linkages also need deeper utilization beyond MoUs.","auditDocumentation":"","__reportArchive":{"category":"internal","auditCycle":"2025-26","version":1},"__administrativeSubmissionStatus":{"deanPlacement":{"submitted":true,"submittedAt":"2026-07-28T11:34:13.981Z","timeZone":"Asia/Kolkata","name":"Dr Arun Sacher","email":"placements@dypiu.ac.in","designation":"Dean Placement","confirmation":{"detailsVerified":true,"documentsUploaded":true}},"dean-placement":{"submitted":true,"submittedAt":"2026-07-28T11:34:13.734819328","name":"Dr Arun Sacher","email":"placements@dypiu.ac.in","userId":243},"registrar":{"submitted":true,"submittedAt":"2026-07-28T11:34:51.239778148","name":"Dr Beeran Moidin B M","email":"registrar@dypiu.ac.in","userId":240},"hr":{"submitted":true,"submittedAt":"2026-07-28T11:35:13.587484740","name":"Ms Hetal Patel","email":"hr@dypiu.ac.in","userId":242},"deanStudentWelfare":{"submitted":true,"submittedAt":"2026-07-28T11:35:59.204Z","timeZone":"Asia/Kolkata","name":"Dr Madhura Jagtap","email":"dean.studentswelfare@dypiu.ac.in","designation":"Dean Student Welfare","confirmation":{"detailsVerified":true,"documentsUploaded":true}},"dean-student-welfare":{"submitted":true,"submittedAt":"2026-07-28T11:35:58.916867602","name":"Dr Madhura Jagtap","email":"dean.studentswelfare@dypiu.ac.in","userId":241}},"__auditSignOff":{"submittedBy":{"name":"","designation":"","role":"","date":"2026-07-28T11:35:58.94468"},"approvedBy":{"name":"","designation":"","role":"","date":""},"auditedBy":{"name":"Dr Abhijeet Digalwar","designation":"External Administrative Auditor","role":"administrative-external-auditor","email":"akd@pilani.bits-pilani1.ac.in","date":"2026-08-13T07:11:03.107Z"}}}	{"coursesOffered":[{"Sr No":"1","Name of the Program":"Bachelor of Technology in Computer Science and Engineering","Level (UG/PG)":"UG","Intake":"1300","No. of Students Admitted":"1291","Year of Commencement of the program":"2019","Attachment (Attach List of the Students)":""},{"Sr No":"2","Name of the Program":"Bachelor of Technology in Semiconductor Engineering","Level (UG/PG)":"UG","Intake":"90\\t","No. of Students Admitted":"77","Year of Commencement of the program":"2024","Attachment (Attach List of the Students)":""},{"Sr No":"3","Name of the Program":"Bachelor of Technology in Mechanical Engineering","Level (UG/PG)":"UG","Intake":"120","No. of Students Admitted":"118","Year of Commencement of the program":"2024","Attachment (Attach List of the Students)":""},{"Sr No":"4","Name of the Program":"Bachelor of Technology in Civil Engineering","Level (UG/PG)":"UG","Intake":"90\\t","No. of Students Admitted":"86","Year of Commencement of the program":"2024","Attachment (Attach List of the Students)":""},{"Sr No":"5","Name of the Program":"Bachelor of Technology in Chemical Engineering","Level (UG/PG)":"UG","Intake":"60","No. of Students Admitted":"52","Year of Commencement of the program":"2024","Attachment (Attach List of the Students)":""},{"Sr No":"6","Name of the Program":"Bachelor of Technology in Bioengineering","Level (UG/PG)":"UG","Intake":"120","No. of Students Admitted":"111","Year of Commencement of the program":"2020","Attachment (Attach List of the Students)":""},{"Sr No":"7","Name of the Program":"Bachelor of Design","Level (UG/PG)":"UG","Intake":"50","No. of Students Admitted":"38","Year of Commencement of the program":"2018","Attachment (Attach List of the Students)":""},{"Sr No":"8","Name of the Program":"Bachelor of Computer Application","Level (UG/PG)":"UG","Intake":"120","No. of 