58	ramendra.pandey@dypiu.ac.in	academic	SOBB	Dr Ramendra Pati Pandey	2026-07-10 13:55:03.311422	APPROVED	Dear Sir / Madam,\n\nPlease go through the observations and recommendations provided by the Internal Auditor and prepare the compliance report to be presented before the External Auditor.\n\nYou are requested to include the compliance report for the observations shared in January 2026, along with the observations and recommendations from the latest Internal Audit Report. \nKindly ensure that the compliance report is complete and supported by the necessary documents/evidence, wherever applicable.	IQAC	2026-07-22 06:10:52.366351	{"schoolName":"School of Biosciences & Bioengineering","establishmentYear":"2018","address":"SOBB, J Block \\\\nD Y Patil International University \\\\nAkurdi, Pune\\\\n","directorName":"Prof. Ramendra Pati Pandey","directorEmail":"ramendra.pandey@dypiu.ac.in","ugIntake":"120","pgIntake":"30","academicCalendar":"Available","bosMeetingsCount":"Three throughout the acdemic year for programs offered by the school","stakeholderFeedback":"Students, Parents and Alumni: The curriculum must incorporate stronger practical and industry-aligned components, provide meaningful entrepreneurship exposure, and integrate advanced technologies, including AI applications in biotechnology. \\\\nFaculty and Academic Experts:  Suggested to incorporate some examples of GMOs and guidelines of government policies and regulation for GENETIC. \\\\n• Suggested changes in syllabus of Biosensor subject  \\\\n  Food certificate and product certification should be separated. Include food packing regulations and techniques of food packaging \\\\nExperts recommended additions in ethical practices and tissue engineering methods. \\\\nIndustry Experts:  suggested Analog Electronics changes and in Digital subject, Biomaterials and Advanced computing for Biological Systems","feedbackAnalysis":"Feedback highlights need for curriculum modernization to ensure graduates possess up-to date competencies aligned with current industrial and  regulatory requirements. \\\\nAcademic experts emphasized content restructuring for conceptual clarity and industry relevance. \\\\nRedundancies identified (e.g., Kosher), and key international standards (Codex Alimentarius) need inclusion for global alignment. ","actionTakenReport":"Syllabus revision committee constituted; latest industrial trends reviewed and necessary updates incorporated into the curriculum. \\\\nCurriculum restructured:  \\\\n• Food certificate and product certification made separate modules.  \\\\n• Food packaging regulations and techniques added as a dedicated unit.  \\\\n• Kosher section removed due to limited academic relevance.  \\\\n• Codex standards incorporated under Food Safety module. \\\\n Existing Biosensors course expanded into “Biosensors and Devices” to enhance instrumentation and application skills. ","foreignCollaborations":"4\\\\n1. Dr. Ramendra Pati Pandey\\\\t\\\\nEvolutionary features of new picorna-like viruses in Culex (Melanoconion) mosquitoes\\\\t\\\\nLilian de Oliveira Guimaraes, Ariel Rocha de Almeida, Endrya do Socorro Foro Ramos, Juliana Telles-de-Deus, Vanessa Christe Helfstein, Vanessa dos Santos Morais, Jesus Maia dos Santos, Vera Lucia Fonseca de Camargo-Neves, Antonio Charlys da Costa, Karin Kirchgatter, Elcio Leal\\\\t\\\\nPasteur Institute, São Paulo, Brazil\\\\n2. Dr. Ramendra Pati Pandey\\\\t\\\\nInsights into drug resistance in Leishmania: Mechanisms, therapeutics, and clinical case studies\\\\t\\\\nGajala Deethamvali Ghousepeer1, Mansi Rani2, Aman Kumar2, Shubhankar Kumar Singh2, Anjali Priyadarshini3, Elcio Leal5, Shailja Singh4, V Samuel Raj3, Subhajit Basu1\\\\t\\\\n1School of Health Science and Technology, UPES, Dehradun, India\\\\n2Indian Council of Medical Research-Rajendra Memorial Research Institute of Medical Science, Patna, India\\\\n3Centre for Drug Design Discovery and Development (C4D), SRM University, Delhi-NCR, India\\\\n4Special Cen