University, Phagwara, Punjab, India.\\\\n\\\\n19. Dr. Suvaithenamudhan S\\\\t\\\\nGenomic analysis identifies unreported adaptive mutations in monkeypox virus immune evasion genes\\\\t\\\\nDr. Saravanan KM\\\\t\\\\nB-Aatral Biosciences Private Limited, Bangalore, India\\\\n\\\\n20. Dr. Pravin Savata Gade\\\\t\\\\nXylooligosaccharide in combination with Lactobacillus rhamnosus ameliorates disturbed circadian rhythm and associated neurological internal desynchronization\\\\t\\\\nRutuja Murlidhar Sonkar, Praveena Bhatt\\\\t\\\\nCSIR-Central Food Technological Research Institute, India\\\\n\\\\n21. Dr. Parth Sarthi Sen Gupta\\\\t\\\\nIntegrated experimental and computational evaluation of novel benzopyran-2-one congeners as reactive oxygen species scavengers in inflammation\\\\t\\\\nAnil K. Saxena\\\\t\\\\nCSIR-CDRI, Lucknow, India\\\\n\\\\n22. Dr. Parth Sarthi Sen Gupta\\\\t\\\\nA simple and sensitive colorimetric biosensor based on three different hydrothermally synthesized AuNP-CQD nanocolloids functionalized with aptamer for the biosensing of diclofenac in serum samples\\\\t\\\\nDr. Sanjay Kumar\\\\t\\\\nNational Forensic Sciences University, Gandhinagar, Gujarat, India","functionalMousCount":"4","__auditSignOff":{"submittedBy":{"name":"Dr Ramendra Pati Pandey","designation":"Director","role":"director","date":"2026-07-10T13:55:02.549Z"},"approvedBy":{"name":"IQAC","designation":"IQAC","role":"iqac","date":"2026-07-22T06:10:52.822Z"},"auditedBy":{"name":"Dr Aniket Kolekar","designation":"Internal Academic Auditor","role":"academic-internal-auditor","date":"2026-07-21T10:53:56.552886654"}},"auditObservations":"1. Documentation and Formatting Issues\\ni. Missing Page Numbers: Reports for Syllabus Revision, NEP 2020 summary, Alumni Interactions, Guest Lectures, Career Guidance, Extension Activities, and Faculty Development all lack page numbers.\\nii. Attendance Incompleteness: Some faculty signatures are missing from the Board of Studies attendance sheets.\\niii. Missing Support Evidence: Valid proofs for student higher studies are missing, and no separate folder exists for placement/higher studies supporting documents.\\niv. Broken Links: Several report links in the \\"Guest Lectures\\" and \\"Faculty Development\\" sections are inaccessible, and a specific PDF for teacher fellowships/financial support failed to open.\\n\\n2. Academic and Operational Discrepancies\\ni. Need to check all feedback dates, all feedbacks must be conducted before BOS. \\nii. The audit identified specific inconsistencies in data reporting and academic ratios:\\nFaculty Count Mismatch: There is a discrepancy in faculty strength reporting, with 19 faculty members listed in the Information tab versus 21 members listed in Part C.\\niii. Student-Teacher Ratio: The current ratio stands at 28.42 (540 students to 19 faculty), which exceeds the recommended limit. The team maintains it must be kept below 25.\\niv. OBE Implementation: The team questioned the methodology for calculating \\"Indirect Attainment\\" and noted the absence of an Action Taken Report (ATR) for the Program Exit Survey.\\n\\n3. Missing Data and Activities\\ni. Research & Publications: Data for Conference Papers was not available, and ISBN/ISSN numbers were missing for several journal papers.\\nii. Student Initiatives: No records were found for Student Startups.\\niii. Financial Records: Proof of consultancy revenue (specifically money deposited by the university to Dr. Parth) was not available.\\niv. Courses: No records were found for the conduct of Value-added or Skill Development courses.\\nv. Professional Bodies: A lack of conducted event reports for 2025-26 for specific professional body associations and student clubs.\\n","auditRecommendations":"1. Motivate the students for Startups\\n2. Maintain the SFR ratio below 1:25\\n3.  Arrange Value-added / Skill Development Courses for the students\\n4. Improve the placement and higher study percentage\\n5. Fetch more consultancy projects\\n6. Student participation in national-level competitions, hackathons, and innovation challenges can be increased.\\n7. Establish a Centre of Excellence in areas such as Biomanufacturing, Functional Foods, Precision Health, or Forensic Genomics \\n","auditDocumentation":[{"name":"sobb review.docx","fileName":"sobb review.docx","url":"/uploads/users/68b4ea08aae4ad01/attachments/c9d73bb1-7273-4fcb-a0be-904ddde6b8c4-sobb_review.docx"},{"name":"SOBB_DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_Template.xlsx","fileName":"SOBB_DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_Template.xlsx","url":"/uploads/users/68b4ea08aae4ad01/attachments/7e4c37db-c6e3-4a36-a89a-cc67f8d179fb-SOBB_DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_Template.xlsx"}],"__reportArchive":{"category":"internal","auditCycle":"2025-26","version":1,"approvedOn":"2026-07-22T06:10:52.822Z"}}	{"studentStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Class":"B. Tech Bioengineering First year","No. of Student":"106","Total":""},{"Sr No":"2","Class":"B. Tech Bioengineering Second year","No. of Student":"59","Total":""},{"Sr No":"3","Class":"B. Tech Bioengineering Third year","No. of Student":"101","Total":""},{"Sr No":"4","Class":"B. Tech Bioengineering Fourth year","No. of Student":"103","Total":""},{"Sr No":"5","Class":"M.Sc Medical Biotechnology First year","No. of Student":"22","Total":""},{"Sr No":"6","Class":"M.Sc Medical Biotechnology Second year","No. of Student":"22","Total":""},{"Sr No":"7","Class":"Total Strength","No. of Student":"","Total":"413"}],"facultyStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Required":"25","Available":"19"}],"boardOfStudies":[{"Sr No":"1","Date of the meeting":"Summary sheet of all BOS meetings","Link for MoM":[{"name":"Summary of BOS meetings SoBB 25-26.pdf","fileName":"Summary of BOS meetings SoBB 25-26.pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/05af65b4cd70cb50/attachments/db1f8ea6-9682-4484-b895-f2a6775fd852-Summary_of_BOS_meetings_SoBB_25-26.pdf"}]}],"syllabusRevision":[{"Sr No":"1","Category of Feedback":"Students Feedb