"-","Duration of MoU":"-","List the actual activities under each MoU":"-","Link to relevant Proof":[{"name":"FunctionalMoUs.pdf","fileName":"FunctionalMoUs.pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/05af65b4cd70cb50/attachments/f7f967ea-61d0-4736-b3dd-76ac63413837-FunctionalMoUs.pdf"},{"name":"FunctionalMoUs.pdf","fileName":"FunctionalMoUs.pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/05af65b4cd70cb50/attachments/a72553cb-9bcb-485a-865f-b0fb2e3380f9-FunctionalMoUs.pdf"}]}],"swocStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Details":"1.\\\\tFaculty members hold PhDs from reputed Indian and international institutions with expertise in disciplines like biotechnology, bioinformatics, criminology, food technology, bioprocess engineering, biomaterial science etc.  2.\\\\tThe school offers Multidisciplinary programs in emerging areas such as Bioengineering, Forensic Science, Medical Biotechnology, and Medicinal Chemistry 3.\\\\tActive research culture with research proposals being submitted to national funding agencies 4.\\\\tWell-equipped laboratories for UG and PG programmes 5.\\\\tCurriculum aligned with NEP 2020 and industry needs 6.\\\\tInterdisciplinary approach encouraged through electives and research 7.\\\\tThe school Organizes national conferences, workshops, FDPs, and student skill-development activities. 8.\\\\tGrowing collaborations with industry and research organizations. 9.\\\\tThe School is a hub bridging together ideas from technology and basic sciences with biology through teaching and research.  10. We encourage students to engage in experiential learning through projects, industry collaborations, and seminars."}],"swocWeaknesses":[{"Sr No":"1","Details":"1.\\\\tNeed for additional specialised faculty in cutting-edge areas like Biomedical instrumentation, Forensic science, Medicinal chemistry 2.\\\\tLimited infrastructure for advanced research, some sophisticated equipments like HR/MS, ICP-OES, Tangential flow filtration unit are required 3.\\\\tLaboratory space constraints with rising student intake 4.\\\\tInadequate computational biology and bioinformatics support 5.\\\\tNeed for increased industry collaborations, consultancy, and technology transfer activities. 6.\\\\tLimited number of patents, technology commercialization, and startup initiatives 7.\\\\tProfessional body activities, guest lectures, and certification programs can be strengthened. 8.\\\\tStudent participation in national-level competitions, hackathons, and innovation challenges can be increased. 9. Stronger industrial participation and more internship opportunities are required."}],"swocOpportunities":[{"Sr No":"1","Details":"1.\\\\tExpand collaborations with industries, hospitals, research institutes, and international universities 2.\\\\tOrganize regular activities under professional bodies, including expert lectures, certification courses, industrial visits, and student chapters 3.\\\\tEstablish Centres of Excellence in areas such as Biomanufacturing, Functional Foods, Precision Health, or Forensic Genomics 4.\\\\tPromote student start-ups, incubation, patent filing, and entrepreneurship through innovation ecosystems 5.\\\\tIncrease consultancy, testing services, and continuing education programs to generate revenue 6.\\\\tStrengthen alumni engagement for placements, internships, mentoring, and research collaborations 7.\\\\tExpansion into futuristic areas: synthetic biology, AI in biology, neurobio, etc.  8.\\\\tPotential to launch interdisciplinary and skill-oriented programmes. 9. Promote the value of undergraduate and graduate research in developing critical thinking, creativity, and problem-solving abilities through undergraduate and graduate students' research and innovation societies, with the goal of promoting and supporting original research and innovation projects carried out by students under faculty mentorship."}],"swocChallenges":[{"Sr No":"1","Details":"1.\\\\tIntense competition from established institutions in attracting quality students and research funding 2.\\\\tSecuring sustained external funding in a highly competitive environment 3.\\\\tKeeping curriculum aligned with rapidly evolving technologies such as AI, synthetic biology, precision medicine, and digital biomanufacturing 4.\\\\tRetaining highly skilled faculty and researchers while balancing teaching, research, and administrative responsibilities 5.\\\\tTranslating laboratory research into commercially viable products and technologies. 6.\\\\tMaintaining high-quality infrastructure and laboratory equipment within budget constraints 7.\\\\tMeeting evolving accreditation, NAAC, NBA, and NIRF expectations while maintaining academic excellence. 8. Challenges in attracting a large number of recruiters for ongoing programs within the school."}],"swocOtherInformation":[{"Sr No":"1","Details":""}]}	[{"name":"sobb review.docx","fileName":"sobb review.docx","url":"/uploads/users/68b4ea08aae4ad01/attachments/c9d73bb1-7273-4fcb-a0be-904ddde6b8c4-sobb_review.docx"},{"name":"SOBB_DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_Template.xlsx","fileName":"SOBB_DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_Template.xlsx","url":"/uploads/users/68b4ea08aae4ad01/attachments/7e4c37db-c6e3-4a36-a89a-cc67f8d179fb-SOBB_DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_Template.xlsx"}]	1	254	Dr Aniket Kolekar	aniket.kolekar@dypiu.ac.in	[254]	["Dr Aniket Kolekar"]	["aniket.kolekar@dypiu.ac.in"]	internal	academic	2026-07-21 08:43:13.250526	Dr Aniket Kolekar	Internal Academic Auditor	academic-internal-auditor	2026-07-21 10:53:56.177751	58	\N	\N	2025-26	INTERNAL	2026-07-22 06:10:52.366328	180	IQAC	iqac	IQAC	\N	t	74	2025-2026	\N	engineering	\N	\N	\N	f	f	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-21 10:53:56.177751	aniket.kolekar@dypiu.ac.in
49	jaiprakash.kalwale@dypiu.ac.in	academic	SOAA	Mr Jaiprakash Kalwale	2026-07-15 05:20:58.182868	APPROVED	Dear Sir / Madam,\n\nPlease go through the observations and recommendations provided by the Internal Auditor and prepare the compliance report to be presented before the External Auditor.\n\nYou are requested to include the compliance report for the observations shared in January 2026, along with the observations and recommendations from the latest Internal Audit Report. \nKindly ensure that the compliance report is complete and supported by the necessary documents/evidence, wherever applicable.	IQAC	2026-07-21 08:48:56.635505	{"schoolName":"School of Applied Arts & Crafts","establishmentYear":"2023 -24","address":"D Y Patil International University, \\nSector 29, Pradhikaran, Akurdi, Pune 411044\\n","directorName":"Jaiprakash G. Kalwale","directorEmail":"director.saac@dypiu.ac.in","ugIntake":"60","pgIntake":"NA","academicCalendar":"Available","bosMeetingsCount":"2","stakeholderFeedback":"28th Nov, 2025 - Not available \\n13th April, 2026 - https://drive.google.com/file/d/1q1sz8_2xR0-AUD-r8yVprCwIlGpkCmCK/view?usp=drive_link","feedbackAnalysis":"28th Nov, 2025 - Not available \\n13th April, 2026 - https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rSb4WWNEWUuWaV4Kq5-b7iKW7JjcvvY_/view?usp=drive_link","actionTakenReport":"28th Nov, 2025 - https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bpmOKMRqIHJ3sR5ZNEvY12liUB_pho1K/view?usp=drive_link \\n13th April, 2026  - https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RjlKFTJ4yIZkFPiQIxYKLtRc-GS0j26E/view?usp=drive_link","foreignCollaborations":"None ","nationalCollaborations":"None","functionalMousCount":"2","__auditSignOff":{"submittedBy":{"name":"Mr Jaiprakash Kalwale","designation":"Director","role":"director","date":"2026-07-15T05:20:57.290Z"},"approvedBy":{"name":"IQAC","designation":"IQAC","role":"iqac","date":"2026-07-21T08:48:56.610Z"},"auditedBy":{"name":"Dr Sandhya Shinde","designation":"Internal Academic Auditor","role":"academic-internal-auditor","date":"2026-07-21T07:32:17.376033235"}},"auditObservations":"1) The School has established the necessary academic processes, including Board of Studies meetings, syllabus revision, Outcome-Based Education (OBE) implementation, mentoring, extension activities, faculty development programmes, and functional MoUs.\\n2) The documentation of several academic activities requires improvement. Supporting evidence such as programme booklets, geotagged photographs, stakeholder feedback, certificates, and accessible file links were missing or incomplete in multiple sections.\\n3) The implementation of Outcome-Based Education needs to be strengthened by incorporating complete CO coverage, attainment analysis, concurrent assessment data, and Action Taken Reports (ATRs) for all courses and semesters.\\n4) Stakeholder feedback analysis requires better documentation. Feedback from all stakeholder categories should be systematically collected, analyzed, and reflected in the syllabus revision process with appropriate supporting evidence.\\n5) Faculty members have participated in FDPs and secured research funding. However, research publications, book chapters, patents, consultancy, corporate training, and collaborative research activities need further enhancement.\\n6) Student support activities such as mentoring, career guidance, extension activities, professional club activities, and student achievements are satisfactory. However, alumni interaction and value-added/skill development courses require greater attention.\\n7) Since the programme is newly established, graduation data, placement statistics, higher studies, student startups, and alumni-related activities are currently Not Applicable.\\n8) Overall, the School demonstrates a positive academic environment with scope for strengthening documentation, research output, industry collaboration, and quality assurance practices.\\n","auditRecommendations":"1) Ensure that all academic records are supported with complete documentary evidence, including programme booklets, geotagged photographs, attendance sheets, stakeholder feedback forms, certificates, and properly accessible file links.\\n2) Strengthen the implementation of Outcome-Based Education by maintaining complete CO-PO attainment records, course exit surveys, concurrent assessment data, question paper mapping, and Action Taken Reports for all courses.\\n3) Establish a structured stakeholder feedback mechanism involving students, alumni, industry experts, employers, and academicians, and incorporate the feedback into syllabus revision with proper documentation.\\n4) Encourage faculty members to publish research papers in reputed Scopus/Web of Science indexed journals with DYPIU affiliation, and promote publications in books, book chapters, conference proceedings, patents, and copyrights.\\n5) Organize value-added courses, skill development programmes, alumni interaction sessions, expert lectures, and industry-oriented training programmes on a regular basis.\\n6) Enhance industry collaboration through additional functional MoUs, consultancy projects, corporate training programmes, internships, and collaborative research initiatives.\\n7) Improve digital documentation by ensuring that all reports, certificates, photographs, and supporting evidence are uploaded with valid and accessible links.\\n8) Motivate students to participate in state-level, national-level, and international-level competitions, exhibitions, innovation challenges, hackathons, and professional certification programmes to enhance their academic and professional competencies.\\n","auditDocumentation":[{"name":"DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_SoAAC.xlsx","fileName":"DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_SoAAC.xlsx","url":"/uploads/users/6bc0cd9ea15f5ffd/attachments/1ff4dc7a-a4cb-46fb-9523-eb8f2c2fc839-DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_SoAAC.xlsx"}],"__reportArchive":{"category":"internal","auditCycle":"2025-26","version":1,"approvedOn":"2026-07-21T08:48:56.610Z"}}	{"studentStrength":[{"Sr N