on ","Link to relevant Proof":[{"name":"MoU- Edualliance Educational Consultants Pvt. Ltd.pdf","fileName":"MoU- Edualliance Educational Consultants Pvt. Ltd.pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/04e09d7ce5a2501c/attachments/35f11f8c-7993-4c62-af8d-cef2525f31c0-MoU-_Edualliance_Educational_Consultants_Pvt._Ltd.pdf"},{"name":"Career Guidance Session Report.pdf","fileName":"Career Guidance Session Report.pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/04e09d7ce5a2501c/attachments/e10e25ff-4008-4759-9355-16594c4fef44-Career_Guidance_Session_Report.pdf"}]}],"swocStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Details":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wuJ_fXVgPnNmm0JfIObLZWMYT5c2xSMX/view?usp=sharing"}],"swocWeaknesses":[{"Sr No":"1","Details":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wuJ_fXVgPnNmm0JfIObLZWMYT5c2xSMX/view?usp=sharing"}],"swocOpportunities":[{"Sr No":"1","Details":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wuJ_fXVgPnNmm0JfIObLZWMYT5c2xSMX/view?usp=sharing"}],"swocChallenges":[{"Sr No":"1","Details":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wuJ_fXVgPnNmm0JfIObLZWMYT5c2xSMX/view?usp=sharing"}],"swocOtherInformation":[{"Sr No":"1","Details":""}]}	[{"name":"DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_SoAAC.xlsx","fileName":"DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_SoAAC.xlsx","url":"/uploads/users/6bc0cd9ea15f5ffd/attachments/1ff4dc7a-a4cb-46fb-9523-eb8f2c2fc839-DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_SoAAC.xlsx"}]	1	251	Dr Sandhya Shinde	sandhya.shinde@dypiu.ac.in	[251]	["Dr Sandhya Shinde"]	["sandhya.shinde@dypiu.ac.in"]	internal	academic	2026-07-21 06:34:11.741361	Dr Sandhya Shinde	Internal Academic Auditor	academic-internal-auditor	2026-07-21 07:32:17.372063	49	\N	\N	2025-26	INTERNAL	2026-07-21 08:48:56.635467	180	IQAC	iqac	IQAC	\N	t	75	2025-2026	\N	nonEngineering	\N	\N	\N	f	f	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-07-21 07:32:17.372063	sandhya.shinde@dypiu.ac.in
51	madhavi.deshpande@dypiu.ac.in	academic	SOCM	Dr Madhavi Deshpande	2026-07-10 16:14:50.98689	APPROVED	Dear Sir / Madam,\n\nPlease go through the observations and recommendations provided by the Internal Auditor and prepare the compliance report to be presented before the External Auditor.\n\nYou are requested to include the compliance report for the observations shared in January 2026, along with the observations and recommendations from the latest Internal Audit Report. \nKindly ensure that the compliance report is complete and supported by the necessary documents/evidence, wherever applicable.	IQAC	2026-07-22 08:48:00.049167	{"schoolName":"School of Commerce and Management","establishmentYear":"2018","address":"Akurdi, Pune","directorName":"Dr. Madhavi Deshpande","directorEmail":"madhavi.deshpande@dypiu.ac.in","ugIntake":"120","pgIntake":"60","academicCalendar":"Available","bosMeetingsCount":"02","stakeholderFeedback":"Feedback on the curriculum was collected from various stakeholders, including academic peers, industry experts, alumni, employers, faculty members,  during the Academic Year 2025–26. Overall, stakeholders appreciated that the curriculum is contemporary, outcome-based, and aligned with industry requirements. They acknowledged the inclusion of emerging areas such as Artificial Intelligence, Business Analytics, Digital Marketing, Sustainability, FinTech, and Industry 4.0/5.0.","feedbackAnalysis":"The feedback was analysed by the Programme Assessment Committee (PAC) and discussed in the Board of Studies (BoS) meetings. The analysis indicated that while the curriculum is relevant and industry-oriented, continuous improvement is essential to meet evolving business and technological requirements.","actionTakenReport":"Based on feedback received from academic peers, alumni, and parents, the School of Commerce and Management undertook several quality enhancement initiatives. The curriculum was reviewed and updated through Board of Studies (BoS) meetings by incorporating academic and industry inputs, with greater emphasis on emerging technologies, practical and experiential learning, and industry relevance. Internship mentoring, industry interactions, guest lectures, workshops, and placement readiness activities were strengthened to enhance students' employability and professional competencies. In addition, the mentor-mentee system, remedial support, counselling, faculty development programmes, and campus facilities were reinforced to improve student learning, well-being, and overall stakeholder satisfaction.","foreignCollaborations":"00","nationalCollaborations":"05","functionalMousCount":"05","__auditSignOff":{"submittedBy":{"name":"Dr Madhavi Deshpande","designation":"Director","role":"director","date":"2026-07-10T16:14:51.538Z"},"approvedBy":{"name":"IQAC","designation":"IQAC","role":"iqac","date":"2026-07-22T08:48:00.474Z"},"auditedBy":{"name":"Dr Vandana Patil","designation":"Internal Academic Auditor","role":"academic-internal-auditor","date":"2026-07-22T08:37:19.477169586"}},"auditObservations":"The School has established a well-structured academic ecosystem supported by effective curriculum planning, Outcome-Based Education (OBE), student mentoring, research initiatives, and quality assurance practices. Academic and administrative records are generally maintained in a systematic manner, reflecting the School's commitment to continuous quality enhancement and institutional excellence. The audit also identified a few areas where documentation, standardization, and evidence-based practices can be further strengthened to align with NAAC quality benchmarks and best practices.\\nObservations:   \\nDuring the verification of the course Fundamentals of Management, a discrepancy was observed in the CO-PO attainment records. The master CO-PO attainment sheet reflects four (4) Course Outcomes, whereas the Examination Section CO-PO attainment sheet reflects five (5) Course Outcomes for the same course. Such inconsistencies may affect the accuracy of outcome attainment analysis and require immediate reconciliation. \\n1.\\tSeveral supporting documents submitted for audit, including mentor–mentee records and other academic documents, were found without the signature and official seal of the School Director/Head of the Department. Proper authentication is essential to establish the validity and authenticity of institutional records. \\n2.\\tFaculty members have contributed to research publications; however, research output is concentrated among a limited number of faculty members. Broader faculty participation in quality publications is necessary to strengthen the School's research profile. \\n3.\\tThe contribution towards Intellectual Property Rights (IPR), including patents, copyrights, design registrations and technology commercialization, remains limited and requires significant improvement. \\n4.\\tIn the Research Funding section, Certificates of Appreciation have been uploaded instead of official research grant sanction letters. Such documents cannot be considered valid evidence of externally funded research projects. \\n5.\\tStartup-related claims require stronger documentary support. The startup summary alone is insufficient for verification. Appropriate documentary evidence such as DPIIT Recognition Certificate, Certificate of Incorporation, Startup India Registration, or an official letter from a recognized incubation centre should be submitted. \\n6.\\tThe School has established effective industry collaborations through functional MoUs with reputed organizations, and various collaborative activities such as guest lectures, internships, industrial visits, and faculty development initiatives have been conducted. However, the MoU documents executed with Icon Overseas, Pune India and Amoeba require verification, as the submitted copies do not bear the official seal of D. Y. Patil International University. Proper authentication of these MoUs is essential to establish their validity and authenticity during academic audit and accreditation processes.\\n","auditRecommendations":"1.\\tVerify and standardize the CO-PO attainment records for all courses to ensure consistency between the approved Course Outcomes, master course files, examination records, and attainment sheets. The discrepancy observed in the course Fundamentals of Management should be rectified by aligning the approved number of Course Outcomes across all academic records. \\n2.\\tEstablish a robust document authentication mechanism by ensuring that all academic and administrative records, including mentor–mentee documents, committee reports, activity reports, and supporting evidence, bear the signature and official seal of the School Director/Head of the Department before submission for audit and accreditation purposes. \\n3.\\tStrengthen faculty research productivity by encouraging equitable participation of all faculty members in publishing research papers in Scopus, Web of Science, ABDC, and other reputed indexed journals through structured research mentoring and periodic performance monitoring. \\n4.\\tEnhance the institutional Innovation and Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) ecosystem by promoting patent filing, copyrights, design registrations, technology transfer, consultancy, and commercialization activities through dedicated institutional support and capacity-building initiatives. \\n5.\\tEnsure submission of valid documentary evidence for funded research projects, including sanction letters, grant approval orders, funding agency communications, and grant release documents. Certificates of appreciation should not be considered as supporting evidence for externally funded research. \\n6.\\tStrengthen the documentation related to startup and innovation activities by maintaining complete supporting records such as DPIIT Recognition Certificates, Startup India Registration, Certificate of Incorporation, incubation agreements, or official communications from recognized incubation centres.\\n7.\\tThe School should ensure that the MoUs executed with Icon Overseas, Pune India and Amoeba are duly authenticated with the signatures of the authorized representatives of both organizations and the official seal of D. Y. Patil International University. Documentary evidence of activities conducted under these MoUs should also be maintained systematically to demonstrate the effectiveness and outcomes of the collaborations.\\n","auditDocumentation":[{"name":"DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_SOCM.xlsx","fileName":"DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_SOCM.xlsx","url":"/uploads/users/e4eb7e89ab03bda0/attachments/77a5102a-31b3-44cc-9c75-5c8987f8a0b3-DYPIU_Academic_Audit_Evaluation_SOCM.xlsx"},{"name":"Observations and recommdations SOCM.docx","fileName":"Observations and recommdations SOCM.docx","url":"/uploads/users/e4eb7e89ab03bda0/attachments/a8d63b8d-8e6c-4b55-9c43-281f7e354219-Observations_and_recommdations_SOCM.docx"}],"__reportArchive":{"category":"internal","auditCycle":"2025-26","version":1,"approvedOn":"2026-07-22T08:48:00.474Z"}}	{"studentStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Class":"BBA Batch 2025-29","No. of Student":"126","Total":"126"},{"Sr No":"2","Class":"BBA Batch 2024-28","No. of Student":"89","Total":"89"},{"Sr No":"3","Class":"BBA Batch 2023-27","No. of Student":"102","Total":"102"},{"Sr No":"4","Class":"MBA Batch 2025-27","No. of Student":"58","Total":"58"},{"Sr No":"5","Class":"MBA Batch 2024-26","No. of Student":"50","Total":"50"}],"facultyStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Required":"24","Available":"17"}],"boardOfStudies":[{"Sr No":"1","Date of the meeting":"9-4-2025 and 6-11-2025 ","Link for MoM":[{"name":"SoCM BOS SUMMARY_Updated (1).pdf","fileName":"SoCM BOS SUMMARY_Updated (1).pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/3dcc0dd157752392/attachments/b265ffe5-a905-4763-a465-c462a635c24f-SoCM_BOS_SUMMARY_Updated__1_.pdf"}]}],"syllabusRevision":[{"Sr No":"1","Category of Feedback":"Academic peer Feedback  Analysis and A