75	jaiprakash.kalwale@dypiu.ac.in	academic	SOAA	Mr Jaiprakash Kalwale	2026-07-28 11:23:29.091035	APPROVED	Dear Sir / Madam,\n\nPlease go through the observations and recommendations provided by the External Auditor of  Academic Audit for AY 2025-26 and prepare the action plan for the recommendations  which will be presented  before the IQAC committee.\n\nKindly ensure that the activities completed are supported by the necessary documents/evidence, wherever applicable.	IQAC	2026-08-13 07:03:00.818296	{"schoolName":"School of Applied Arts & Crafts","establishmentYear":"2023 -24","address":"D Y Patil International University, \\nSector 29, Pradhikaran, Akurdi, Pune 411044\\n","directorName":"Jaiprakash G. Kalwale","directorEmail":"director.saac@dypiu.ac.in","ugIntake":"60","pgIntake":"NA","academicCalendar":"Available","bosMeetingsCount":"2","stakeholderFeedback":"28th Nov, 2025 - Not available \\n13th April, 2026 - https://drive.google.com/file/d/1q1sz8_2xR0-AUD-r8yVprCwIlGpkCmCK/view?usp=drive_link","feedbackAnalysis":"28th Nov, 2025 - Not available \\n13th April, 2026 - https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rSb4WWNEWUuWaV4Kq5-b7iKW7JjcvvY_/view?usp=drive_link","actionTakenReport":"28th Nov, 2025 - https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bpmOKMRqIHJ3sR5ZNEvY12liUB_pho1K/view?usp=drive_link \\n13th April, 2026  - https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RjlKFTJ4yIZkFPiQIxYKLtRc-GS0j26E/view?usp=drive_link","foreignCollaborations":"None ","nationalCollaborations":"None","functionalMousCount":"2","auditObservations":"The School of Applied Art and Craft provides a creative academic environment that nurtures artistic expression, craftsmanship, visual communication, and applied design skills. The School possesses dedicated studios and practical learning facilities that enable students to acquire professional competencies through hands-on training. Faculty members actively encourage participation in exhibitions, competitions, and creative projects. The curriculum reflects the traditional strengths of applied arts while gradually incorporating contemporary practices. However, greater integration with digital technologies, industry engagement, entrepreneurship, and systematic academic quality assurance would significantly enhance the School's overall academic profile.\\n\\nIt was observed that the documentation of all the activities is very poor and need standardization. School need to prepare all the documentation in standard format as expected by the accreditation and ranking authorities.","auditRecommendations":"• Strengthen Outcome-Based Education by establishing measurable learning outcomes, systematic CO–PO mapping, attainment analysis, and continuous quality improvement.\\n• Modernize the curriculum by integrating Digital Illustration, Digital Media, Animation, Motion Graphics, AR/VR Applications, Creative Technologies, Digital Photography, and AI-assisted Art Practices.\\n• Expand collaborations with advertising agencies, design firms, publishing houses, museums, cultural organizations, and creative industries.\\n• Encourage entrepreneurship by supporting student startups, independent studios, freelancing skills, and creative business management.\\n• Develop interdisciplinary projects involving Design, Engineering, Media, Architecture, and Biosciences.\\n• Upgrade studio infrastructure with modern digital art laboratories, printing technologies, photography studios, and multimedia production facilities.\\n• Promote faculty and student participation in national and international exhibitions, competitions, workshops, and collaborative projects.\\n• Strengthen research and scholarly contributions in visual communication, art education, indigenous crafts, and creative innovation.\\n• Improve documentation of exhibitions, student portfolios, outreach activities, and Action Taken Reports (ATRs) arising from stakeholder feedback.\\n• Establish structured alumni and industry mentoring programmes to improve employability, internships, and professional networking.\\n•  School need to work extensively on improving the documentation of all the activities  including Board of Studies meetings, syllabus revision, Outcome-Based Education (OBE) implementation, mentoring, extension activities, faculty development programmes, functional MoUs etc.","auditDocumentation":[],"__reportArchive":{"category":"external","auditCycle":"2025-26","version":2,"approvedOn":"2026-08-13T07:03:00.906Z"},"__auditSignOff":{"submittedBy":{"name":"Mr Jaiprakash Kalwale","designation":"Director","role":"director","date":"2026-07-28T11:23:30.076Z"},"approvedBy":{"name":"IQAC","designation":"IQAC","role":"iqac","date":"2026-08-13T07:03:00.906Z"},"auditedBy":{"name":"Dr Abhijeet Digalwar","designation":"External Academic Auditor","role":"academic-external-auditor","date":"2026-08-13T05:03:28.689731800"}}}	{"studentStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Class":"First Year","No. of Student":"41","Total":"41"},{"Sr No":"2","Class":"Second Year","No. of Student":"45","Total":"45"},{"Sr No":"3","Class":"Third Year","No. of Student":"48","Total":"48"},{"Sr No":"4","Class":"Final Year","No. of Student":"NA","Total":"NA"}],"facultyStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Required":"15","Available":"8"}],"boardOfStudies":[{"Sr No":"1","Date of the meeting":"13th April, 2026 ","Link for MoM":[{"name":"MOM (1).pdf","fileName":"MOM (1).pdf","url":"/uploads/users/04e09d7ce5a2501c/attachments/38bfd003-b311-4c36-8481-2f93b29f3f0f-MOM__1_.pdf"}]},{"Sr No":"2","Date of the meeting":"28th Nov, 2025","Link for MoM":[{"name":"MOM.pdf","fileName":"MOM.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/04e09d7ce5a2501c/attachments/780971c0-5f67-48a5-ab31-7fc8addedbb6-MOM.pdf"}]}],"syllabusRevision":[{"Sr No":"1","Category of Feedback":"Faculty Feedback 2026 ","Link for Analysis and ATR":[{"name":"DYPIU faculty feedback.pdf","fileName":"DYPIU faculty feedback.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/04e09d7ce5a2501c/attachments/9305ace0-3c14-49f8-a3a5-ea6cd3caa301-DYPIU_faculty_feedback.pdf"}]},{"Sr No":"2","Category of Feedback":"Parents Fee