nctioned.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/05af65b4cd70cb50/attachments/7b23e5c8-f073-4aab-a4f6-4dd2f5a5a29f-ResearchFundsSanctioned.pdf"},{"name":"E-content.pdf","fileName":"E-content.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/05af65b4cd70cb50/attachments/eaaa4c93-2194-492b-b42b-bbb7e2f278cf-E-content.pdf"},{"name":"Awards.pdf","fileName":"Awards.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/05af65b4cd70cb50/attachments/3160c8f8-112a-4df9-b7f7-404f485ab2a4-Awards.pdf"},{"name":"Patents.pdf","fileName":"Patents.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/05af65b4cd70cb50/attachments/cddc2749-db78-4dc7-b8d7-12efc437e94d-Patents.pdf"},{"name":"SeminarConfFDPOrganised.pdf","fileName":"SeminarConfFDPOrganised.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/05af65b4cd70cb50/attachments/55464a22-05a4-4f2a-9ce4-17846cff0d65-SeminarConfFDPOrganised.pdf"},{"name":"SeminarConfFDPAttended.pdf","fileName":"SeminarConfFDPAttended.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/05af65b4cd70cb50/attachments/471bbe78-eeb9-4758-9593-558f37307f68-SeminarConfFDPAttended.pdf"},{"name":"FunctionalMoUs.pdf","fileName":"FunctionalMoUs.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/05af65b4cd70cb50/attachments/f7f967ea-61d0-4736-b3dd-76ac63413837-FunctionalMoUs.pdf"},{"name":"FunctionalMoUs.pdf","fileName":"FunctionalMoUs.pdf","url":"/uploads/users/05af65b4cd70cb50/attachments/a72553cb-9bcb-485a-865f-b0fb2e3380f9-FunctionalMoUs.pdf"}]	2	263	Dr Abhijeet Digalwar	akd@pilani.bits-pilani.ac.in	[263]	["Dr Abhijeet Digalwar"]	["akd@pilani.bits-pilani.ac.in"]	external	academic	2026-07-28 11:22:09.371499	Dr Abhijeet Digalwar	External Academic Auditor	academic-external-auditor	2026-08-13 04:55:50.706557	58	58	58	2025-26	EXTERNAL	2026-08-13 07:03:12.165753	180	IQAC	iqac	IQAC	1	f	\N	2025-2026	\N	engineering	\N	\N	\N	f	f	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-08-13 04:55:50.709961	akd@pilani.bits-pilani.ac.in
76	arvind.kumar@dypiu.ac.in	academic	SOMCS	Dr Arvind Kumar	2026-07-28 11:25:39.600198	APPROVED	Dear Sir / Madam,\n\nPlease go through the observations and recommendations provided by the External Auditor and prepare the compliance report for the same.\n\nPlease prepare an action plan to implement the suggestions of the Experts and submit it to IQAC by 8th August 2026.\n\nKindly ensure that the compliance report is complete and supported by the necessary documents/evidence, wherever applicable.	IQAC	2026-07-31 10:21:56.564425	{"schoolName":"School of Media & Communication Studies ","establishmentYear":"2018","address":"School of Media & Communication Studies, J Block, D Y Patil International University, Akurdi, Pune. ","directorName":"Dr. Arvind Kumar","directorEmail":"arvind.kumar@dypiu.ac.in","ugIntake":"60","pgIntake":"","academicCalendar":"Not Available","bosMeetingsCount":"3","stakeholderFeedback":"❖\\\\tFaculty Feedback \\\\n●\\\\tMost of the teachers are satisfied with the overall structure of the curriculum. \\\\n●\\\\tCertain courses may be revised by replacing subjects such as Technical Communication Skills with more contemporary, skill-based courses, considering that students are now technologically savvy.\\\\n●\\\\tThe curriculum should place greater emphasis on emerging skills aligned with current technological advancements.\\\\n●\\\\tIncreased focus on evolving industry requirements is essential to ensure that students are industry-ready upon completion of their education.\\\\n\\\\n❖\\\\tAlumni Feedback \\\\n●\\\\tMaximum students are satisfied with the nature of the curriculum. \\\\n●\\\\t30% of students said that there has to be more skill based courses to meet the industry needs. \\\\n●\\\\tSome students said, more courses can be offered in the domain of communication management. \\\\n\\\\n❖\\\\tEmployers’ Feedback \\\\n●\\\\tGreater emphasis should be placed on practical, hands-on assignments, with a corresponding reduction in excessive theoretical components, to strengthen experiential learning.\\\\n●\\\\tThe curriculum, which is currently largely journalism-centric, should be broadened to support diverse career pathways beyond traditional journalism, enabling students to pursue varied professional roles.\\\\n●\\\\tIntroduction of more industry-oriented practical courses—such as Advanced Excel, Power BI, query languages, technical writing, and data-related tools—would better prepare students for entry into the corporate sector.\\\\n●\\\\tSpecialized pathways may be explored, such as enabling students of Advertising and Public Relations specialisation to engage with sector-specific industries like real estate and allied domains.\\\\n●\\\\tNew courses on Crisis Communication, Risk Management, and reporting on sensitive and confidential issues should be incorporated to enhance professional communication competence and ethical preparedness.\\\\n●\\\\tContinuous evolution and upgradation of the curriculum in line with changing industry requirements is essential to maintain relevance and ensure students remain industry-ready, while also providing ample writing practice to strengthen critical thinking skills.\\\\n","feedbackAnalysis":"Feedback from faculty, alumni, and employers indicates overall satisfaction with the curriculum structure, while highlighting the need for strategic enhancement. Faculty members recommend revising select courses by introducing contemporary, skill-based subjects aligned with technological advancements and evolving industry needs. Alumni feedback reflects general satisfaction, though nearly 30% emphasised the inclusion of more skill-oriented and communication management courses. Employers strongly advocated for increased practical exposure, reduced theoretical load, and diversification beyond a journalism-centric approach. They also suggested introducing industry-relevant tools, sector-specific pathways, and courses on crisis communication and risk management. Collectively, the feedback underscores the importance of continuous curriculum upgradation to ensure industry readiness and relevance.","actionTakenReport":"Based on the comprehensive feedback received from faculty members, alumni, and employers, the Board of Studies has undertaken targeted curriculum enhancements to strengthen industry relevance and skill orientation. In response to suggestions for introducing contemporary, technology-driven skills, a new skill enhancement course titled “UX Writing” has been introduced. This course is designed to equip students with practical competencies in user-centric content creation, digital communication, and interface writing, thereby addressing emerging industry requirements beyond traditional journalism roles.\\\\nAdditionally, select modules across existing courses have been revised to incorporate greater practical exposure, updated tools, and application-based learning outcomes. Emphasis has been placed on aligning content with current industry practices, improving hands-on assignments, and enhancing employability skills. These revisions aim to reduce excessive theoretical focus while fostering experiential learning and critical thinking. The implemented changes reflect a proactive approach towards continuous curriculum upgradation, ensuring that students are better prepared for diverse career pathways in the evolving media and communication landscape.","foreignCollaborations":"NA","nationalCollaborations":"The Film Appreciation Course was organized by the School of Media and Journalism, D Y Patil International University, in collaboration with the 'Film and Television Institute of India'. The collaboration brought together experienced faculty members and film professionals to deliver a structured academic program on cinema studies. It enabled students to benefit from expert-led sessions, interdisciplinary learning, and exposure to contemporary approaches in film appreciation, strengthening the academic and practical understanding of cinema as an art form and medium of communication.\\\\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1y9Ws8cmtBGot2gLTjhdd4CY_A61ODyM4/view?usp=sharing \\\\n","functionalMousCount":"4","auditObservations":"The School of Media and Communication Studies (SMCS) has established the basic academic framework for delivering its BA JMC and MA JMC programs and has initiated various academic and quality assurance processes. Teaching staff is well qualified and has vast industry exposure. School has its own Radio Channel. The School has also recognized the importance of experiential learning by incorporating practical assignments, skill-based training, and exposure to digital media tools as part of its academic delivery.","auditRecommendations":"The audit revealed several areas requiring focused attention to enhance institutional effectiveness and academic quality. The Vision and Mission statements require comprehensive revision, as they do not clearly differentiate between the School's long-term aspirations and the strategies for achieving them. Student admissions were observed to be comparatively low, with nearly 50% of the approved intake being filled, indicating the need for stronger outreach and branding initiatives. The implementation of Outcome-Based Education (OBE) requires significant strengthening, particularly in faculty understanding of outcome formulation, CO–PO mapping, attainment analysis, and continuous improvement practices. The feedback collection and analysis mechanism needs to be supported by well-documented Action Taken Reports (ATRs). Similarly, the process for identifying slow and advanced learners lacks a structured methodology, with limited documentary evidence of interventions and their effectiveness. The overall quality of documentation also requires improvement, as inconsistencies were observed in maintaining supporting records; in a few instances, event reports were not authenticated with the signatures of the respective coordinators or responsible authorities.","auditDocumentation":[],"__reportArchive":{"category":"external","auditCycle":"2025-26","version":2,"approvedOn":"2026-07-31T10:21:57.129Z"},"__auditSignOff":{"submittedBy":{"name":"Dr Arvind Kumar","designation":"Director","role":"director","date":"2026-07-28T11:25:40.612Z"},"approvedBy":{"name":"IQAC","designation":"IQAC","role":"iqac","date":"2026-07-31T10:21:57.129Z"},"auditedBy":{"name":"Dr Arun Sharma","designation":"External Academic Auditor","role":"academic-external-auditor","date":"2026-07-30T19:51:21.128505299"}}}	{"studentStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Class":"1st Year BAJMC","No. of Student":"29","Total":"90"},{"Sr No":"2","Class":"2nd Year BAJMC ","No. of Student":"30","Total":"90"},{"Sr No":"3","Class":"3rd Year BAJMC ","No. of Student":"31","Total":"90"}],"facultyStrength":[{"Sr No":"1","Required":"0","Available":"9"}],"boardOfStudies":[{"Sr No":"1","Date of the meeting":"All","Link for MoM":[{"name":"SoMCS BOS SUMMARY.pdf","fileName":"SoMCS BOS SUMMARY.pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/bd7f66e8f7af62de/attachments/46736a5a-2dbb-4311-a4e9-e9b9b386db4f-SoMCS_BOS_SUMMARY.pdf"}]}],"syllabusRevision":[{"Sr No":"1","Category of Feedback":"All","Link for Analysis and ATR":[{"name":"Part A -2- SoMCS SUMMARY Sheet.pdf","fileName":"Part A -2- SoMCS SUMMARY Sheet.pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/bd7f66e8f7af62de/attachments/21655662-4ee2-468c-b2fe-d13e5c6e8412-Part_A_-2-_SoMCS_SUMMARY_Sheet.pdf"}]}],"obeImplementation":[{"Sr No":"1","Particular":"Learning Outcomes","Link for the Document":[{"name":"Part A -3-1 SoMCS SUMMARY Sheet.pdf","fileName":"Part A -3-1 SoMCS SUMMARY Sheet.pdf","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/dypiu-schoolappraisal-uploads/users/bd7f66e8f7af62de/attachments/b46d3fc0-b2c8-46d3-89e8-aaf43578cfc9-Part_A_-3-1_SoMCS_SUMMARY_Sheet.pdf"}]},{"Sr No":"2","Particular":"Concurrent Assessment","Link for the Document":[{"name":"Part A -3-2 SoMCS SUMMARY Sheet.pdf","fileName"