73	sunil.talekar@dypiu.ac.in	academic	SOD	Dr Sunil Talekar	2026-07-28 11:16:51.796159	APPROVED	Dear Sir / Madam,\n\nPlease go through the observations and recommendations provided by the External Auditor of  Academic Audit for AY 2025-26 and prepare the action plan for the recommendations  which will be presented  before the IQAC committee.\n\nKindly ensure that the activities completed are supported by the necessary documents/evidence, wherever applicable.	IQAC	2026-08-13 07:02:51.114324	{"schoolName":"School of Design ","establishmentYear":"2018-19","address":"School of Design, J Block, D. Y. Patil International University, Sector 29, Akurdi, Pune, Maharashtra. Pin - 411044.","directorName":"Dr. Sunil Talekar ","directorEmail":"sunil.talekar@dypiu.ac.in","ugIntake":"60","pgIntake":"NA","academicCalendar":"Available","bosMeetingsCount":"2","stakeholderFeedback":"Done- https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1ZK_0F_BCX4_yAuJlnPltwUiYR-Tfg7mt/edit?usp=drive_link&ouid=111933864758971274888&rtpof=true&sd=true","feedbackAnalysis":"Done- https://docs.google.com/document/d/11SaBhLHUHp-n3MURRvEqlXjS2--OywMF/edit?usp=drive_link&ouid=111933864758971274888&rtpof=true&sd=true","actionTakenReport":"Done- https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ypm2-QBWACJzSSJt65OdaGBngvY1MOiw/view?usp=drive_link\\n\\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1-ZW2fG2Wk0ZwlOS23uouH6SvfYzzlv84/edit?usp=drive_link&ouid=111933864758971274888&rtpof=true&sd=true\\n","foreignCollaborations":"-","nationalCollaborations":"-","functionalMousCount":"3","auditObservations":"The School of Design has established an innovative academic environment that encourages creativity, design thinking, and experiential learning. The School offers students opportunities to engage in practical design studios, project-based learning, and multidisciplinary activities. Faculty members demonstrate strong academic and professional competence, while available infrastructure supports various design disciplines. The School has initiated collaborations with industry and promotes creative expression through exhibitions and student projects. Nevertheless, greater emphasis is required on research, international exposure, industry-sponsored studios, and systematic quality assurance processes to further strengthen academic excellence. \\n\\nThe documentation of the school is not up to the mark as expected by the accreditation authorities. School need to work on the same.","auditRecommendations":"• Strengthen the implementation of OBE with clearly defined Programme Outcomes, systematic CO–PO mapping, attainment analysis, and continuous improvement mechanisms.\\n• Revise the curriculum by incorporating emerging areas such as Human-Centered Design, UX/UI Design, Service Design, Sustainable Design, AI-assisted Design, Design Analytics, and Design Entrepreneurship.\\n• Increase industry-sponsored live projects, design consultancy assignments, and collaborative studio-based learning.\\n• Strengthen interdisciplinary collaboration with Engineering, Biosciences, and Applied Arts programmes through integrated design projects.\\n• Upgrade digital fabrication laboratories, prototyping facilities, AR/VR studios, and advanced visualization technologies.\\n• Introduce structured portfolio assessment and external jury evaluation at every academic level.\\n• Enhance research activities in design innovation, user experience, sustainability, and creative technologies through funded projects and publications.\\n• Promote international collaborations, student exchange programmes, global design competitions, and visiting faculty lectures.\\n• Strengthen alumni engagement in mentoring, internships, placement support, and curriculum review.\\n• Improve documentation of student achievements, exhibitions, outreach activities, and quality assurance processes as an outcome.","auditDocumentation":[],"__reportArchive":{"category":"external","auditCycle":"2025-26","version":2,"approvedOn":"2026-08-13T07:02:51.186Z"},"__auditSignOff":{"submi